{"header":{"numFound":142,"maxScore":16.93852,"queryTime":908,"page":1,"pageSize":10},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Yogo Bekti Firmanto","name":"Yogo Bekti","surname":"Firmanto","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ahmadi Ahmadi","name":"Ahmadi","surname":"Ahmadi","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Rangsang Purnama","name":"Rangsang","surname":"Purnama","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Wiwiet Herulambang","name":"Wiwiet","surname":"Herulambang","rank":4,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0211 other engineering and technologies"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0202 electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"02 engineering and technology"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"7. Clean energy"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Battery Health Monitoring System Lithium-Ion Based on Fuzzy Logic","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Batteries that can store electrical energy and are easy to carry make them the most practical technology choice as an electricity source. Even so, lithium-ion batteries are not free from the risk of damage when used. Therefore, a Lithium-ion battery health monitoring system was created. This system uses the INA219 sensor as a current and voltage detector and the DS18B20 sensor as a temperature detector. Arduino as a data process. The test results show that all components function well. In battery capacity testing, the highest error was 1.8%. For the DS18B20 sensor as a temperature sensor, an error of 2.4% was obtained. Testing capacity against temperature on the battery when the temperature was 25 C, the current was 485mAh; when the temperature was 44.8 C, the current was 550mAh, there was a difference of 65mAh or 11%. This difference corresponds to the difference in battery capacity. Testing using the Fuzzy Logic method was carried out on 3 batteries with different capacities to obtain the State of Health (SOH) value for each battery. Testing is carried out in real-time, as well as Matlab simulation. In battery test 1, with a capacity of 2200mAh and the highest temperature of 32.1 oC, the device's State of Health (SoH) was 90%, and Fuzzy Matlab was 87.6%. Battery 2, 1500mAh capacity with the highest temperature of 33.4oC obtained State of Health (SOH) of 60%, Fuzzy Matlab 60%. Battery 3 Capacity 2200mAh, Highest temperature 32.2 oC, State of Health (SOH) of 90%, Fuzzy Matlab 87.6%. The test results show that the overall error is still below 5%. A properly functioning Internet of Things (IoT) system can display information on lithium-ion batteries' State of Health (SoH) on devices and smartphones.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-06-30","publisher":"Communicator Sphere Fakultas Ilmu Sosial dan Ilmu Politik Program Studi Ilmu Komunikasi Universitas Bhayangkara Surabaya","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"JEECS (Journal of Electrical Engineering and Computer Sciences)","issnPrinted":"2528-0260","issnOnline":"2579-5392","issnLinking":null,"ep":"30","iss":null,"sp":"19","vol":"9","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::8880b0a68fffda1f1bac05c396b4f41b","originalIds":["10.54732/jeecs.v9i1.3","50|doiboost____|8880b0a68fffda1f1bac05c396b4f41b"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.54732/jeecs.v9i1.3"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":1.0,"influence":2.2522935E-9,"popularity":2.6041114E-9,"impulse":1.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Faculty of Engineering","acronym":"Faculty of Engineering","id":"pending_org_::e9f241666450683af4f36d061a9ceefb","pids":null,"countries":[{"code":"UNKNOWN","label":"Unknown"}],"websiteurl":null},{"legalName":"Universitas Bhayangkara Surabaya","acronym":"Universitas Bhayangkara Surabaya","id":"openorgs____::a579750cec25143da5a210504794336c","pids":[{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02kycr729"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q12523302"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000403858811"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.444386.9"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q12523302"}],"countries":[{"code":"ID","label":"Indonesia"}],"websiteurl":"https://www.ubhara.ac.id"},{"legalName":"Facualty of Engineering","acronym":"Facualty of Engineering","id":"pending_org_::e0484a842bb99c764068cabb51cba9f7","pids":null,"countries":[{"code":"UNKNOWN","label":"Unknown"}],"websiteurl":null}],"communities":[{"code":"energy-planning","label":"Energy Planning","provenance":null}],"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.54732/jeecs.v9i1.3"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.54732/jeecs.v9i1.3"],"publicationDate":"2024-06-30","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::e7c6a7adfb4692692414cce17c1cb380","value":"Journal of Electrical Engineering and Computer Sciences"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::b9b34e3b19250cdb27d84ae1443f7675","fullName":"Marco Ströbel","name":"Marco","surname":"Ströbel","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-5921-8747"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::e035ce5e0ac9a6ee08cf9a1e8bb60c64","fullName":"Larissa Kiefer","name":"Larissa","surname":"Kiefer","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0007-7285-8902"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Kai Peter Birke","name":"Kai Peter","surname":"Birke","rank":3,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"DE","label":"Germany","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"acetyltributylcitrate"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"TK1001-1841"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"600"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"7. Clean energy"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0104 chemical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"increased thermal stability of electrolytes"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"TP250-261"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"621.3"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"ecofriendly electrolyte for lithium-ion batteries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Production of electric energy or power. Powerplants. Central stations"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Industrial electrochemistry"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"enhanced electrolyte safety based on high flash point"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"tributylacetylcitrate"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Investigation of a Novel Ecofriendly Electrolyte-Solvent for Lithium-Ion Batteries with Increased Thermal Stability","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>This study presents tributyl acetylcitrate (TBAC) as a novel ecofriendly high flash point and high boiling point solvent for electrolytes in lithium-ion batteries. The flash point (TFP=217∘C) and the boiling point (TBP=331∘C) of TBAC are approximately 200 K greater than that of conventional linear carbonate components, such as ethyl methyl carbonate (EMC) or diethyl carbonate (DEC). The melting point (TMP=−80∘C) is more than 100 K lower than that of ethylene carbonate (EC). Furthermore, TBAC is known as an ecofriendly solvent from other industrial sectors. A life cycle test of a graphite/NCM cell with 1 M lithium hexafluorophosphate (LiPF6) in TBAC:EC:EMC:DEC (60:15:5:20 wt) achieved a coulombic efficiency of above 99% and the remaining capacity resulted in 90 percent after 100 cycles (C/4) of testing. As a result, TBAC is considered a viable option for improving the thermal stability of lithium-ion batteries.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2021-10-28","publisher":"MDPI AG","embargoEndDate":"2022-01-19","sources":["Crossref","Batteries, Vol 7, Iss 4, p 72 (2021)","Batteries","Volume 7","Issue 4","Pages: 72"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Batteries","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2313-0105","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"72","vol":"7","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::3b297dab5bc1ebf562bf1984b8257194","originalIds":["batteries7040072","10.3390/batteries7040072","50|doibo